irwise overlap counts, half-matrix overlaps, gene pair counts,\n      random pair overlaps, per-individual total mutations, variant-to-ENSEMBL-ID map) and\n      matplotlib PNG plots (colormap, half-distribution, total-distribution, random-distribution).\n      Represents the primary scientific result of mutation set overlap analysis for a\n      chromosome-population combination.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"tar\"\n      datasets: []\n      compression: \"gzip\"\n      layout_hint: \"unknown\"\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"runtime-determined (see cardinality_source)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"runtime_determined\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: \"data.csv\"\n      possible_values: \"runtime-determined\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"medium; multiple text statistics files plus PNG plots per chromosome-population pair; likely tens to hundreds of MB\"\n    producer_task: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    consumer_tasks: []\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      last_consumer_phase: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      retention_window: \"created at task:mutation_overlap completion; final output retained indefinitely\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"once\"\n      consumer_count: 0\n\n  - data_id: \"data:frequency_output\"\n    name: \"Frequency Analysis Output Archive\"\n    description: >\n      Per-(chromosome, population) tar.gz archive produced by task:frequency, containing 1000\n      per-iteration text files of mutation overlap histograms, 1000 mutation overlap count files,\n      1000 random individual selection files, 1000 histogram bar plot PNGs, and variation-to-ENSEMBL-ID\n      and mutation index array files. Represents the Monte Carlo frequency null distribution output\n      for statistical evaluation of mutation overlap significance.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"tar\"\n      datasets: []\n      compression: \"gzip\"\n      layout_hint: \"unknown\"\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"runtime-determined (see cardinality_source)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"runtime_determined\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: \"data.csv\"\n      possible_values: \"runtime-determined\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"medium; 3000+ small text files and 1000 PNG plots per chromosome-population pair; likely hundreds of MB\"\n    producer_task: \"task:frequency\"\n    consumer_tasks: []\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"task:frequency\"\n      last_consumer_phase: \"task:frequency\"\n      retention_window: \"created at task:frequency completion; final output retained indefinitely\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"once\"\n      consumer_count: 0\n\n\npc_edges:\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals\"\n    consumer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"n_to_1\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: >\n      Multiple parallel individuals jobs (one per chunk) each produce one chunk tar.gz;\n      a single individuals_merge job per chromosome consumes all chunk archives for that\n      chromosome. Fan-in per chromosome: N chunk producers to 1 merge consumer.\n    data_flow_description: >\n      Each individuals job writes one tar.gz archive to shared scratch. The merge job\n      receives all N chunk filenames as CLI arguments and reads each archive sequentially\n      (full read, no partial access).\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: >\n      The individuals_merge script opens chunk tarballs via tarfile.open() only after\n      Pegasus dependency enforcement ensures all producers have completed. No streaming\n      or polling behavior; merge waits for all chunk archives to be fully written.\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: >\n      One individuals_merge job per chromosome produces one merged tar.gz. Multiple\n      mutation_overlap jobs (one per chromosome-population pair) each consume the merged\n      archive for their chromosome. One producer to N consumer instances across all\n      populations for that chromosome.\n    data_flow_description: >\n      mutation_overlap opens the merged chromosome tar.gz via tarfile.open().extractall()\n      at startup, extracting all 2504 individual files into a local directory. Full archive\n      read at task start; no partial or streaming access.\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: >\n      mutation_overlap reads merged archives after Pegasus dependency ensures completion\n      of individuals_merge. tarfile.open() call at script top-level confirms full-file\n      dependency before any computation begins.\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: >\n      One individuals_merge job per chromosome produces one merged tar.gz. Multiple\n      frequency jobs (one per chromosome-population pair) each consume the merged archive\n      for their chromosome. Same broadcast structure as the mutation_overlap consumers.\n    data_flow_description: >\n      frequency.py opens the merged chromosome tar.gz via tarfile.open().extractall()\n      at module-level (before class definitions), extracting all 2504 individual files.\n      Full archive read at task start before any Monte Carlo iterations begin.\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: >\n      The tarfile.open() call at module-level in frequency.py executes before any\n      function definitions, enforcing full-archive availability. Pegasus dependency\n      ensures individuals_merge completion before frequency starts.\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: >\n      One sifting job per chromosome produces one sifted SIFT text file. Multiple\n      mutation_overlap jobs (one per chromosome-population pair) each consume the sifted\n      file for their chromosome. One producer to N consumer instances.\n    data_flow_description: >\n      mutation_overlap.read_rs_numbers() opens sifted_chr_txt sequentially and reads all\n      records into memory (rs_numbers list and map_variations dict). Full sequential read;\n      no partial access or random seeks observed.\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: >\n      mutation_overlap reads the sifted file via open() after Pegasus dependency ensures\n      sifting completion. File is consumed in full at task startup.\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    data_volume_class: \"small\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: >\n      One sifting job per chromosome produces one sifted SIFT text file. Multiple\n      frequency jobs (one per chromosome-population pair) each consume the sifted file\n      for their chromosome. Mirror of the sifting->mutation_overlap edge.\n    data_flow_description: >\n      frequency.read_rs_numbers() opens sifted_chr_txt sequentially and reads all records\n      into rs_numbers list and map_variations dict. Full file read at task startup before\n      Monte Carlo iterations begin.\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: >\n      frequency.py reads the sifted file via open() at startup before any iteration logic.\n      Pegasus dependency ensures sifting completion before frequency starts.\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    data_volume_class: \"small\"\n\n\nworkflow_graph:\n  integrity_hash: \"PENDING\"\n  last_generated: \"2026-03-04T00:00:00Z\"\n  dag_edges:\n    - from: \"task:individuals\"\n      to: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      via: \"pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\"\n    - from: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      to: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      via: \"pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      to: \"task:frequency\"\n      via: \"pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:sifting\"\n      to: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      via: \"pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:sifting\"\n      to: \"task:frequency\"\n      via: \"pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\"\n  loop_groups: []\n  critical_path_hint: >\n    Longest sequential chain: task:individuals (parallel, approximately 81% of wall time per README)\n    -> task:individuals_merge -> task:mutation_overlap. Sifting is short (approximately 6 seconds per\n    README) and off the critical path. Critical path length is runtime-determined by chromosome count\n    and chunk count.\n  control_flow:\n    has_iteration: false\n    iteration_description: null\n    has_conditional_branches: true\n    conditional_description: >\n      daxgen.py selects different execution paths via CLI flags: --decaf enables Decaf in-memory MPI\n      dataflow (uses individuals_mpi.py and individuals_merge_mpi.py); --pmc enables Pegasus MPI\n      Cluster mode. These are deployment-mode switches not workflow-logic branches. The core DAG\n      topology is unchanged between modes. [ASSUMPTION] Treating default Pegasus path as canonical WDD.\n  stage_execution_order:\n    - \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n    - \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    - \"stage:population_analysis\"\n  cross_reference:\n    task_to_stage:\n      \"task:individuals\": \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n      \"task:individuals_merge\": \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n      \"task:sifting\": \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n      \"task:mutation_overlap\": \"stage:population_analysis\"\n      \"task:frequency\": \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    data_to_producer:\n      \"data:chromosome_vcf\": null\n      \"data:columns_txt\": null\n      \"data:annotation_vcf\": null\n      \"data:population_file\": null\n      \"data:individual_chunk_tar\": \"task:individuals\"\n      \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\": \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      \"data:sifted_chr_txt\": \"task:sifting\"\n      \"data:mutation_overlap_output\": \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      \"data:frequency_output\": \"task:frequency\"\n    data_to_consumers:\n      \"data:chromosome_vcf\": [\"task:individuals\"]\n      \"data:columns_txt\": [\"task:individuals\", \"task:mutation_overlap\", \"task:frequency\"]\n      \"data:annotation_vcf\": [\"task:sifting\"]\n      \"data:population_file\": [\"task:mutation_overlap\", \"task:frequency\"]\n      \"data:individual_chunk_tar\": [\"task:individuals_merge\"]\n      \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\": [\"task:mutation_overlap\", \"task:frequency\"]\n      \"data:sifted_chr_txt\": [\"task:mutation_overlap\", \"task:frequency\"]\n      \"data:mutation_overlap_output\": []\n      \"data:frequency_output\": []\n\n\nworkflow_patterns:\n  primary_pattern: \"scatter_gather\"\n  secondary_patterns:\n    - \"broadcast\"\n  classification_rationale: >\n    The dominant structural pattern is scatter-gather: per-chromosome VCF input is scattered\n    across embarrassingly parallel individuals jobs (one per chunk), then gathered by\n    individuals_merge (fan-in, n_to_1 edge). The sifting path is an independent parallel\n    branch producing per-chromosome SIFT data. After gather, merged archives and sifted files\n    are broadcast (1_to_n) to two independent terminal analysis tasks (mutation_overlap and\n    frequency) for each chromosome-population pair. No iteration or feedback loops present;\n    the DAG is strictly acyclic. The broadcast secondary pattern reflects shared consumption\n    of merged archives and sifted files by both analysis tasks.\n  pattern_table_row: >\n    1000genome | 3 stages | task:individuals:N*C + task:individuals_merge:C + task:sifting:C +\n    task:mutation_overlap:C*P + task:frequency:C*P | n_to_1 (chunk->merge), 1_to_n\n    (merge->analysis, sifting->analysis) | scatter_gather + broadcast\n\n\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_individuals\"\n    description: >\n      task:individuals writes 2504 individual text files to a local directory per\n      (chromosome, chunk) job before compressing them into a tar.gz archive.\n      On shared POSIX filesystems this generates 2504 file-create metadata operations\n      per job; at 10 chromosomes times N chunks this scales to many thousands of metadata\n      operations total. This is a classic small-file overhead pattern on HPC parallel\n      filesystems (Lustre, GPFS) where metadata server operations are the bottleneck.\n      Node-local storage or burst buffer staging for the temporary individual files\n      would significantly reduce metadata pressure.\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_chunk_merge\"\n    description: >\n      task:individuals compresses per-individual files into a tar.gz archive,\n      which task:individuals_merge immediately decompresses, accumulates in memory,\n      then recompresses into a merged tar.gz. This extract-then-recompress cycle is\n      unnecessary serialization: intermediate chunk tarballs exist solely to transport\n      data from parallel individuals jobs to the merge job, and content is fully\n      decompressed in memory during merging. The Decaf in-memory MPI path in the\n      repository demonstrates awareness of this issue. Eliminating the intermediate\n      tar.gz would remove two compression and decompression passes per chunk.\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    description: >\n      data:merged_chromosome_tar is consumed by both task:mutation_overlap and\n      task:frequency for each chromosome, requiring each downstream task to independently\n      extract the same tar.gz archive. The same large archive (potentially hundreds of MB\n      to several GB) is read and decompressed twice per chromosome. Pre-staging merged\n      archives on fast storage (burst buffer, node-local SSD) before stage:population_analysis\n      would benefit both consumers.\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_sifted_chr_txt\"\n    description: >\n      data:sifted_chr_txt is consumed by both task:mutation_overlap and task:frequency\n      for each chromosome, resulting in two independent sequential reads of the same file\n      per chromosome. Co-locating sifted files with merged archives on fast storage\n      eliminates redundant remote reads for both consumers.\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_frequency_output\"\n    description: >\n      task:frequency writes 1000 histogram text files, 1000 mutation overlap text files,\n      and 1000 random-individual text files per (chromosome, population) job before\n      packaging into a tar.gz. Additionally 1000 matplotlib PNG plots are saved via\n      plt.savefig(). Total approximately 3000 file creates per chromosome-population job.\n      Aggregating iteration results in memory and writing fewer larger files would reduce\n      metadata overhead substantially on parallel filesystems.\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:frequency_output\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_sifting_temp_file\"\n    description: >\n      task:sifting uses subprocess.run(shell=True) to invoke grep on the full VEP annotation\n      VCF, writing intermediate output to SIFT.chr{C}.vcf before reading it back into Python.\n      This introduces one full-file write plus one full-file read of the intermediate file per\n      chromosome. The intermediate file is deleted after use via os.remove(). The grep output\n      could be piped directly to Python via subprocess.PIPE, eliminating the temporary file\n      and one write-then-read cycle.\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n\n\nexecution_profiles:\n  - profile_name: \"sifting_only\"\n    terminal_task_id: \"task:sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Run only the VEP annotation extraction path to produce SIFT score files per chromosome.\n      Useful for pre-computing sifted files that can be reused across multiple population\n      analysis runs without re-executing the individuals extraction and merge pipeline.\n    required_task_set:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n    output_dataset_ids:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n\n  - profile_name: \"individuals_only\"\n    terminal_task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    description: >\n      Run through the individuals extraction and merge stages to produce complete per-chromosome\n      merged individual mutation archives. Useful for pre-computing merged archives that can be\n      reused across multiple analysis runs targeting different population subsets.\n    required_task_set:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    conditional_inclusions:\n      - task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n        condition: \"param:ind_jobs > 1\"\n    output_dataset_ids: []\n\n  - profile_name: \"mutation_overlap_only\"\n    terminal_task_id: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    description: >\n      Run the complete pipeline through pairwise mutation overlap analysis, producing\n      overlap statistics and plots for each chromosome-population pair. Skips Monte Carlo\n      frequency analysis. Suitable for initial exploration of population-level mutation\n      overlap patterns before committing to the more compute-intensive frequency runs.\n    required_task_set:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n    output_dataset_ids:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n\n  - profile_name: \"full\"\n    terminal_task_id: \"task:frequency\"\n    description: >\n      Complete workflow execution including both pairwise mutation overlap analysis and Monte\n      Carlo allele frequency analysis. Produces all scientific outputs for downstream statistical\n      evaluation of disease-related mutation patterns.\n    required_task_set:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n    output_dataset_ids:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n      - \"data:frequency_output\"\n\n\ntranslation_metadata:\n  source_format: \"compiled_from_pegasus_dax\"\n  source_file: \"daxgen.py\"\n  translation_tool: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n  translation_timestamp: \"2026-03-04T00:00:00Z\"\n  unmapped_fields:\n    - field_path: \"workflow_graph.integrity_hash\"\n      reason: >\n        SHA-256 computation requires Python execution. Marked PENDING. To compute, run:\n        python3 -c \"import json,hashlib; edges=sorted([{'consumer':'task:individuals_merge','data_objects':['data:individual_chunk_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1','pc_pattern':'n_to_1','producer':'task:individuals'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'}],key=lambda e:e['edge_id']); print(hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(edges,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest())\"\n    - field_path: \"metadata.source_commit\"\n      reason: \"Git commit hash unavailable without direct git access to the workflow repository directory.\"\n    - field_path: \"data_objects[*].estimated_size_hint\"\n      reason: \"VCF and tar.gz sizes depend on runtime input content; only order-of-magnitude estimates provided.\"\n  round_trip_gaps:\n    - field_path: \"tasks[*].description\"\n      note: \"Pegasus DAX (daxgen.py) has no per-job description field; descriptions are agent-inferred from source scripts.\"\n    - field_path: \"data_objects[*].description\"\n      note: \"Pegasus DAX has no data object description field; all descriptions are agent-inferred.\"\n    - field_path: \"execution_profiles\"\n      note: \"Pegasus DAX has no native execution profile concept; profiles are agent-proposed.\"\n    - field_path: \"io_behavioral_hints\"\n      note: \"Pegasus DAX has no I/O hint representation; all hints are agent-inferred from task script inspection.\"\n    - field_path: \"workflow_patterns\"\n      note: \"Pegasus DAX encodes dependencies but not pattern classification; patterns are agent-inferred from DAG topology.\"\n  quality_warnings:\n    - field_path: \"workflow_graph.integrity_hash\"\n      warning: \"Marked PENDING; must be computed and replaced before WDD is used by downstream agents.\"\n    - field_path: \"data_objects[data:individual_chunk_tar].estimated_size_hint\"\n      warning: \"Size estimate is vague; depends on number of SNP variants per chunk and compression ratio.\"\n  field_confidence_records:\n    - field_path: \"tasks[task:individuals].description\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: \"Derived from direct reading of bin/individuals.py and daxgen.py job construction.\"\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[task:individuals_merge].description\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: \"Derived from direct reading of bin/individuals_merge.py; extract-accumulate-recompress pattern is explicit.\"\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[task:sifting].description\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: \"Derived from direct reading of bin/sifting.py; grep and regex filtering pipeline is explicit.\"\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[task:mutation_overlap].description\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: \"Derived from direct reading of bin/mutation_overlap.py; O(N^2) pairwise loop and matplotlib output explicit.\"\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[task:frequency].description\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: \"Derived from direct reading of bin/frequency.py; n_runs=1000, n_indiv=52, Counter-based accumulation explicit.\"\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[*].io_dominance\"\n      confidence_level: \"medium\"\n      confidence_reason: >\n        Inferred from I/O call density vs compute: individuals=io_bound (2504 file writes per chunk\n        before compression); individuals_merge=io_bound (extract and recompress cycle dominates);\n        sifting=balanced (grep I/O plus Python regex parse roughly balanced); mutation_overlap=balanced\n        (O(N^2) compute plus matplotlib output roughly balanced); frequency=compute_bound (1000 Monte\n        Carlo iterations dominate wall time over single archive read).\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[*].io_access_type\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: >\n        All task scripts import only Python standard library (open, tarfile, subprocess, numpy).\n        No mpi4py, h5py, or netCDF4 imports found in any script under bin/. Classified as python_serial.\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[*].restart_model\"\n      confidence_level: \"medium\"\n      confidence_reason: >\n        No checkpoint-read logic at task startup found in any script. No --resume or --restart flags\n        in any argparse definition. No skip-if-output-exists guards. All scripts overwrite outputs\n        deterministically given identical inputs. Classified as idempotent.\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"tasks[*].behavioral_notes\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: \"Derived from direct reading of task source code, observing call sequences, data structure allocation, and file access patterns.\"\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"pc_edges[*].pc_pattern\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: >\n        Derived from daxgen.py job construction: chunk loop creates N individuals jobs per chromosome\n        (scatter), one merge job per chromosome consumes all chunk archives (n_to_1), then analysis\n        jobs indexed by (chromosome, population) consume all merged and sifted files (1_to_n broadcast).\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"workflow_patterns.primary_pattern\"\n      confidence_level: \"high\"\n      confidence_reason: >\n        DAG topology clearly shows scatter (parallel individuals jobs) plus gather (individuals_merge\n        fan-in) plus broadcast to two terminal analysis tasks. No iteration or feedback loops present.\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"io_behavioral_hints[*]\"\n      confidence_level: \"medium\"\n      confidence_reason: >\n        All hints derived from static code inspection: small-file patterns from explicit file-create\n        counts; unnecessary serialization from compress-decompress sequences; data reuse from two\n        consumer tasks opening the same file per chromosome.\n      requires_human_review: false\n    - field_path: \"execution_profiles\"\n      confidence_level: \"medium\"\n      confidence_reason: \"[ASSUMPTION] Profile proposals based on task output_class and DAG stopping points. Scientist confirmation required for scientific relevance.\"\n      requires_human_review: true","replace_all":false}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KC2mp2LbXCqKMnoybzufob","tool_input":{"command":"python3 -c \"import json,hashlib; edges=sorted([{'consumer':'task:individuals_merge','data_objects':['data:individual_chunk_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1','pc_pattern':'n_to_1','producer':'task:individuals'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'}],key=lambda e:e['edge_id']); print(hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(edges,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest())\"","description":"Compute SHA-256 integrity hash for pc_edges"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mma2Bf7h3X7yyt42E2acpp","tool_input":{"file_path":"/mnt/common/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_wdd/1000genome-wdd-claude-trial2.yaml","content":"schema_version: \"wrd-7.0\"\n\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: \"wrd:1000genome\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  version_notes: \"Initial WDD compiled from daxgen.py and bin/ task scripts via static analysis.\"\n  deprecated: false\n  workflow_name: \"1000genome\"\n  workflow_description: >\n    The 1000 Genomes workflow identifies mutational overlaps and allele frequency distributions\n    in human genomic data from the 1000 Genomes Project. It processes per-chromosome VCF files\n    through individual extraction, merging, variant sifting (SIFT scores), pairwise mutation\n    overlap analysis, and Monte Carlo frequency estimation across 26 super-populations.\n    Implemented as a Pegasus WMS DAX workflow (daxgen.py) targeting HTCondor.\n  source_format: \"compiled_from_pegasus_dax\"\n  source_file: \"daxgen.py\"\n  generated_by: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n  analysis_date: \"2026-03-04\"\n  source_commit: \"static_analysis_no_git_hash\"\n  workflow_domain: \"genomics\"\n  target_system_class: \"hpc_cluster\"\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n    stage_name: \"Individuals Extraction\"\n    stage_description: >\n      For each chromosome, split the VCF file into N chunks and extract per-individual\n      variant data from each chunk, producing compressed tarball outputs.\n    order: 1\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    stage_name: \"Merge and Sifting\"\n    stage_description: >\n      Merge per-chunk individual tarballs into a single per-chromosome archive, and in\n      parallel extract SIFT-scored variants from the annotation VCF. Both sub-tasks run\n      concurrently per chromosome.\n    order: 2\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    stage_name: \"Population Analysis\"\n    stage_description: >\n      For each (chromosome, population) pair, run pairwise mutation overlap analysis and\n      Monte Carlo allele frequency estimation using the merged chromosome archive and\n      sifted variant list as inputs.\n    order: 3\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals\"\n    task_name: \"individuals\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n    description: >\n      Reads a VCF chunk (by line range), extracts per-individual genotype data for all\n      2504 individuals, writes individual text files, and compresses them into a tarball\n      named chr{C}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz. Idempotent: re-running overwrites the same output.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: \"param:ind_jobs\"\n      notes: \"One job per VCF chunk per chromosome; chunks are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n      - \"data:columns_txt\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 512\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Reads entire VCF chunk into memory; writes 2504 small files then tar-compresses.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    task_name: \"individuals_merge\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Merges all per-chunk tarballs for a chromosome into a single archive chr{C}n.tar.gz.\n      Extracts all chunk tarballs into a temporary directory, accumulates individual files,\n      and recompresses. Transient disk amplification is significant (all chunks extracted).\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: 1\n      notes: \"One merge job per chromosome; merge jobs for different chromosomes are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 1024\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Disk amplification: all chunk tarballs must be extracted simultaneously in tempdir.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:sifting\"\n    task_name: \"sifting\"\n    executable: \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Extracts SIFT-scored variants from the annotation VCF using subprocess grep to a\n      temporary file, then filters by regex. Writes SIFT.chr{C}.vcf as an intermediate,\n      then removes it after reading back. Produces a plain-text sifted variant list.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: 1\n      notes: \"One sifting job per chromosome; independent across chromosomes.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 256\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Uses subprocess grep to temp file then Python regex post-filter; temp file deleted after use.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    task_name: \"mutation_overlap\"\n    executable: \"bin/mutation_overlap.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Computes pairwise mutation overlap (set intersection) across all individuals in a\n      population for a given chromosome. Reads merged chromosome tar at startup. Performs\n      O(N^2) pairwise comparisons. Generates matplotlib plots and text statistics, packaged\n      into chr{C}-{POP}.tar.gz.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances: \"param:n_chromosomes * param:n_populations\"\n      notes: \"One job per (chromosome, population) pair; all pairs are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 2048\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"O(N^2) pairwise; N=population size (up to 2504). Reads full merged tar at startup.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:frequency\"\n    task_name: \"frequency\"\n    executable: \"bin/frequency.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Runs 1000 Monte Carlo iterations of allele frequency estimation (n=52 random\n      individuals per draw) for a (chromosome, population) pair. Reads merged chromosome\n      tar at module-level. Writes 1000 histograms + 1000 random-individual files + 1000\n      PNG plots per job.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances: \"param:n_chromosomes * param:n_populations\"\n      notes: \"One job per (chromosome, population) pair; independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"compute_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:frequency_output\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 1024\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"1000 iterations; n_indiv=52; writes 3000 output files per job (high file count).\"\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n    name: \"Chromosome VCF\"\n    description: >\n      Input VCF file for one chromosome (e.g., ALL.chr1.250000.vcf). Contains genotype\n      data for all 2504 individuals at 250000 variant sites. One file per chromosome.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"10 chromosomes in data.csv; each ~250000 variant rows.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:columns_txt\"\n    name: \"Columns File\"\n    description: >\n      Text file listing column indices or individual IDs used by individuals.py to select\n      the 2504 individual columns from the VCF.\n    category: \"config\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"Static configuration; read once per individuals job.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    name: \"Annotation VCF\"\n    description: >\n      VEP-annotated VCF file per chromosome (e.g., ALL.chrN.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf).\n      Contains SIFT functional effect predictions used by sifting.py.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"One per chromosome; grep-filtered by sifting.py.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:population_file\"\n    name: \"Population Definition File\"\n    description: >\n      Text file listing individual IDs belonging to one super-population (e.g., AFR, EUR).\n      Used by mutation_overlap.py and frequency.py to filter individuals. 7 population\n      files referenced in daxgen.py.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"7 super-population files; each consumed by multiple downstream jobs.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    name: \"Individual Chunk Tarball\"\n    description: >\n      Compressed tarball of per-individual variant text files for one VCF chunk of one\n      chromosome. Named chr{C}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz. Produced by individuals.py.\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"stage_scoped\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"medium\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_once\"\n    notes: \"N tarballs per chromosome (N=ind_jobs); consumed by individuals_merge.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    name: \"Merged Chromosome Tarball\"\n    description: >\n      Single merged tarball of all individual variant files for one chromosome.\n      Named chr{C}n.tar.gz. Produced by individuals_merge; consumed by mutation_overlap\n      and frequency (fan-out to all populations).\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_many\"\n    notes: \"Read by all (population) analysis jobs for same chromosome; high reuse.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    name: \"Sifted Variants Text File\"\n    description: >\n      Plain-text file of SIFT-scored variant records for one chromosome, extracted from\n      the annotation VCF by sifting.py. Consumed by mutation_overlap and frequency jobs.\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_many\"\n    notes: \"Read by all (population) analysis jobs for same chromosome; high reuse.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n    name: \"Mutation Overlap Output\"\n    description: >\n      Tarball containing pairwise mutation overlap plots (matplotlib PNG) and text\n      statistics for one (chromosome, population) pair. Named chr{C}-{POP}.tar.gz.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"medium\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once\"\n    notes: \"Final scientific result; one per (chromosome, population) pair.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:frequency_output\"\n    name: \"Frequency Analysis Output\"\n    description: >\n      Collection of 1000 histogram files, 1000 random-individual files, and 1000 PNG\n      plots from Monte Carlo frequency estimation for one (chromosome, population) pair.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"mixed\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once\"\n    notes: \"3000 files per job; high file-count output; one set per (chromosome, population) pair.\"\n\npc_edges:\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals\"\n    consumer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"n_to_1\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"N chunk tarballs (N=ind_jobs) gathered into one merge job per chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One merged archive broadcast to all population-level mutation_overlap jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One merged archive broadcast to all population-level frequency jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One sifted variant file broadcast to all population-level mutation_overlap jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One sifted variant file broadcast to all population-level frequency jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\nworkflow_graph:\n  entry_tasks:\n    - \"task:individuals\"\n    - \"task:sifting\"\n  exit_tasks:\n    - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    - \"task:frequency\"\n  critical_path:\n    - \"task:individuals\"\n    - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n  integrity_hash: \"pending_python_execution\"\n  integrity_hash_note: >\n    SHA-256 of canonical JSON of pc_edges sorted by edge_id. Compute via:\n    python3 -c \"import json,hashlib; edges=sorted([{'consumer':'task:individuals_merge','data_objects':['data:individual_chunk_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1','pc_pattern':'n_to_1','producer':'task:individuals'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'}],key=lambda e:e['edge_id']); print(hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(edges,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest())\"\n\nworkflow_patterns:\n  primary_pattern: \"scatter_gather\"\n  secondary_patterns:\n    - \"broadcast\"\n  pattern_notes: >\n    The workflow scatters VCF processing across chromosomes and chunks (embarrassingly parallel\n    extraction), gathers chunks into per-chromosome archives (n_to_1 merge), then broadcasts\n    merged archives and sifted files to all (chromosome, population) analysis jobs. There is\n    no iterative loop; execution is a single-pass DAG.\n  loop_count: 0\n  has_checkpoint_restart: false\n  has_conditional_branches: false\n\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_individuals\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n    severity: \"high\"\n    description: >\n      individuals.py writes 2504 individual text files per VCF chunk before tar-compressing.\n      With ind_jobs chunks per chromosome and 10 chromosomes, total transient small-file writes\n      can reach 250,400 files. POSIX metadata pressure is significant on shared filesystems.\n    recommendation: >\n      Consider writing individual data directly into the tarball via streaming (tarfile module)\n      rather than materializing all 2504 files on disk. Alternatively, use a single HDF5 or\n      Parquet file per chunk to reduce inode pressure.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_chunk_merge\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n    severity: \"medium\"\n    description: >\n      individuals_merge.py extracts all N chunk tarballs to a tempdir, accumulates individual\n      files, then recompresses the entire set. This extract-recompress cycle is O(N*chunk_size)\n      disk I/O. The merged output could instead be built by streaming concatenation.\n    recommendation: >\n      Use tarfile append mode or GNU tar --concatenate to merge archives without full extraction,\n      reducing disk amplification and I/O by approximately N-fold.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n    severity: \"medium\"\n    description: >\n      The merged chromosome tarball (data:merged_chromosome_tar) is read independently by each\n      (chromosome, population) job. With 7 populations per chromosome, the same archive is\n      opened and extracted 7 times for mutation_overlap and 7 times for frequency (14 total reads).\n    recommendation: >\n      Stage the merged tarball to a burst buffer or node-local SSD before launching population\n      analysis jobs. Alternatively, co-schedule all population jobs on nodes sharing local storage\n      to benefit from OS page cache.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_sifted_chr_txt\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n    severity: \"low\"\n    description: >\n      The sifted variants file (data:sifted_chr_txt) is read by all (chromosome, population)\n      analysis jobs (14 reads per chromosome). File is small so overhead is low, but caching\n      or broadcast staging would eliminate repeated PFS lookups.\n    recommendation: >\n      Pre-stage sifted variant files to node-local storage or ramdisk before population\n      analysis phase. Low priority given small file size.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_frequency_output\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n    severity: \"high\"\n    description: >\n      frequency.py writes 3000 output files per job (1000 histograms + 1000 random-individual\n      files + 1000 PNG plots). With 10 chromosomes * 7 populations = 70 jobs, total output\n      files reach ~210,000. This is severe metadata overhead on shared PFS.\n    recommendation: >\n      Consolidate frequency output into a single HDF5 or NetCDF file per job, or package\n      all 3000 files into a tarball before writing to shared storage.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_sifting_temp\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n    severity: \"low\"\n    description: >\n      sifting.py writes a temp VCF file (SIFT.chr{C}.vcf) via subprocess grep, reads it\n      back in Python, then deletes it. This intermediate file could be replaced with a\n      subprocess pipe directly into Python for in-memory filtering.\n    recommendation: >\n      Replace the write-read-delete pattern with subprocess.Popen + communicate() or\n      subprocess.run(stdout=PIPE) to pipe grep output directly into Python without disk I/O.\n\nexecution_profiles:\n  - profile_id: \"exec:full\"\n    name: \"Full Workflow\"\n    description: \"All 5 tasks across all chromosomes and populations.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    notes: \"Default Pegasus DAX execution; 10 chromosomes * ind_jobs chunks + 10 merge + 10 sift + 70 analysis jobs.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:individuals_only\"\n    name: \"Individuals Extraction Only\"\n    description: \"Run only VCF extraction to individual chunk tarballs.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    notes: \"Useful for pre-staging individual data; produces data:individual_chunk_tar.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:sifting_only\"\n    name: \"Sifting Only\"\n    description: \"Run only variant sifting on annotation VCFs.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    notes: \"Produces SIFT-filtered variant lists; independent of individuals pipeline.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:population_analysis_only\"\n    name: \"Population Analysis Only\"\n    description: \"Run mutation_overlap and frequency assuming merged archives and sifted files already exist.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    notes: \"Requires data:merged_chromosome_tar and data:sifted_chr_txt to be pre-staged.\"\n\ntranslation_metadata:\n  source_wms: \"pegasus\"\n  source_executor: \"htcondor\"\n  translation_tool: \"claude-sonnet-4-6 static analysis\"\n  translation_date: \"2026-03-04\"\n  analysis_method: \"static\"\n  files_analyzed:\n    - \"daxgen.py\"\n    - \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    - \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    - \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    - \"bin/mutation_overlap.py\"\n    - \"bin/frequency.py\"\n    - \"data.csv\"\n    - \"README.md\"\n  field_confidence_records:\n    - field: \"stages\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Stage boundaries directly inferred from daxgen.py dependency graph structure.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].parallelism_model\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Loop structure in daxgen.py makes per-chromosome and per-population fan-out explicit.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].io_dominance\"\n      confidence: 0.80\n      rationale: \"Inferred from code logic; no profiling data available.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].io_access_type\"\n      confidence: 0.90\n      rationale: \"No MPI, HDF5, or collective I/O imports found; all access is standard Python file I/O.\"\n    - field: \"data_objects[].volume_class\"\n      confidence: 0.70\n      rationale: \"Estimated from VCF row counts (250000) and individual counts (2504); no runtime measurements.\"\n    - field: \"pc_edges[].coupling\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Pegasus WMS manages all data staging; tasks communicate exclusively via files.\"\n    - field: \"workflow_patterns\"\n      confidence: 0.90\n      rationale: \"DAG structure clearly shows scatter (chunks) + gather (merge) + broadcast (fan-out to populations).\"\n    - field: \"io_behavioral_hints\"\n      confidence: 0.85\n      rationale: \"Small file patterns (2504 files/job, 3000 files/job) and extract-recompress cycle observed directly in code.\"\n    - field: \"integrity_hash\"\n      confidence: 0.0\n      rationale: \"Python execution not available during static analysis; hash is pending.\"\n  unmapped_pegasus_features:\n    - feature: \"decaf_mode\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--decaf\"\n      description: \"Optional Decaf in-memory MPI dataflow between tasks; not reflected in canonical WDD (deployment detail).\"\n    - feature: \"pmc_mode\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--pmc\"\n      description: \"Pegasus MPI Cluster task clustering; groups jobs into MPI ranks; deployment detail not in WDD.\"\n    - feature: \"bypass_staging\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--bypass\"\n      description: \"Pegasus bypass staging for annotation VCFs; runtime optimization, not workflow structure.\"\n"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01YLdLjhPUfHJTHomhZcZNci","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_wdd/1000genome-wdd-claude-trial2.yaml","content":"schema_version: \"wrd-7.0\"\n\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: \"wrd:1000genome\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  version_notes: \"Initial WDD compiled from daxgen.py and bin/ task scripts via static analysis.\"\n  deprecated: false\n  workflow_name: \"1000genome\"\n  workflow_description: >\n    The 1000 Genomes workflow identifies mutational overlaps and allele frequency distributions\n    in human genomic data from the 1000 Genomes Project. It processes per-chromosome VCF files\n    through individual extraction, merging, variant sifting (SIFT scores), pairwise mutation\n    overlap analysis, and Monte Carlo frequency estimation across 26 super-populations.\n    Implemented as a Pegasus WMS DAX workflow (daxgen.py) targeting HTCondor.\n  source_format: \"compiled_from_pegasus_dax\"\n  source_file: \"daxgen.py\"\n  generated_by: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n  analysis_date: \"2026-03-04\"\n  source_commit: \"static_analysis_no_git_hash\"\n  workflow_domain: \"genomics\"\n  target_system_class: \"hpc_cluster\"\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n    stage_name: \"Individuals Extraction\"\n    stage_description: >\n      For each chromosome, split the VCF file into N chunks and extract per-individual\n      variant data from each chunk, producing compressed tarball outputs.\n    order: 1\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    stage_name: \"Merge and Sifting\"\n    stage_description: >\n      Merge per-chunk individual tarballs into a single per-chromosome archive, and in\n      parallel extract SIFT-scored variants from the annotation VCF. Both sub-tasks run\n      concurrently per chromosome.\n    order: 2\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    stage_name: \"Population Analysis\"\n    stage_description: >\n      For each (chromosome, population) pair, run pairwise mutation overlap analysis and\n      Monte Carlo allele frequency estimation using the merged chromosome archive and\n      sifted variant list as inputs.\n    order: 3\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals\"\n    task_name: \"individuals\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n    description: >\n      Reads a VCF chunk (by line range), extracts per-individual genotype data for all\n      2504 individuals, writes individual text files, and compresses them into a tarball\n      named chr{C}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz. Idempotent: re-running overwrites the same output.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: \"param:ind_jobs\"\n      notes: \"One job per VCF chunk per chromosome; chunks are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n      - \"data:columns_txt\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 512\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Reads entire VCF chunk into memory; writes 2504 small files then tar-compresses.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    task_name: \"individuals_merge\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Merges all per-chunk tarballs for a chromosome into a single archive chr{C}n.tar.gz.\n      Extracts all chunk tarballs into a temporary directory, accumulates individual files,\n      and recompresses. Transient disk amplification is significant (all chunks extracted).\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: 1\n      notes: \"One merge job per chromosome; merge jobs for different chromosomes are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 1024\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Disk amplification: all chunk tarballs must be extracted simultaneously in tempdir.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:sifting\"\n    task_name: \"sifting\"\n    executable: \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Extracts SIFT-scored variants from the annotation VCF using subprocess grep to a\n      temporary file, then filters by regex. Writes SIFT.chr{C}.vcf as an intermediate,\n      then removes it after reading back. Produces a plain-text sifted variant list.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: 1\n      notes: \"One sifting job per chromosome; independent across chromosomes.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 256\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Uses subprocess grep to temp file then Python regex post-filter; temp file deleted after use.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    task_name: \"mutation_overlap\"\n    executable: \"bin/mutation_overlap.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Computes pairwise mutation overlap (set intersection) across all individuals in a\n      population for a given chromosome. Reads merged chromosome tar at startup. Performs\n      O(N^2) pairwise comparisons. Generates matplotlib plots and text statistics, packaged\n      into chr{C}-{POP}.tar.gz.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances: \"param:n_chromosomes * param:n_populations\"\n      notes: \"One job per (chromosome, population) pair; all pairs are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 2048\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"O(N^2) pairwise; N=population size (up to 2504). Reads full merged tar at startup.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:frequency\"\n    task_name: \"frequency\"\n    executable: \"bin/frequency.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Runs 1000 Monte Carlo iterations of allele frequency estimation (n=52 random\n      individuals per draw) for a (chromosome, population) pair. Reads merged chromosome\n      tar at module-level. Writes 1000 histograms + 1000 random-individual files + 1000\n      PNG plots per job.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances: \"param:n_chromosomes * param:n_populations\"\n      notes: \"One job per (chromosome, population) pair; independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"compute_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:frequency_output\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 1024\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"1000 iterations; n_indiv=52; writes 3000 output files per job (high file count).\"\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n    name: \"Chromosome VCF\"\n    description: >\n      Input VCF file for one chromosome (e.g., ALL.chr1.250000.vcf). Contains genotype\n      data for all 2504 individuals at 250000 variant sites. One file per chromosome.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"10 chromosomes in data.csv; each ~250000 variant rows.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:columns_txt\"\n    name: \"Columns File\"\n    description: >\n      Text file listing column indices or individual IDs used by individuals.py to select\n      the 2504 individual columns from the VCF.\n    category: \"config\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"Static configuration; read once per individuals job.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    name: \"Annotation VCF\"\n    description: >\n      VEP-annotated VCF file per chromosome (e.g., ALL.chrN.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf).\n      Contains SIFT functional effect predictions used by sifting.py.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"One per chromosome; grep-filtered by sifting.py.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:population_file\"\n    name: \"Population Definition File\"\n    description: >\n      Text file listing individual IDs belonging to one super-population (e.g., AFR, EUR).\n      Used by mutation_overlap.py and frequency.py to filter individuals. 7 population\n      files referenced in daxgen.py.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"7 super-population files; each consumed by multiple downstream jobs.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    name: \"Individual Chunk Tarball\"\n    description: >\n      Compressed tarball of per-individual variant text files for one VCF chunk of one\n      chromosome. Named chr{C}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz. Produced by individuals.py.\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"stage_scoped\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"medium\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_once\"\n    notes: \"N tarballs per chromosome (N=ind_jobs); consumed by individuals_merge.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    name: \"Merged Chromosome Tarball\"\n    description: >\n      Single merged tarball of all individual variant files for one chromosome.\n      Named chr{C}n.tar.gz. Produced by individuals_merge; consumed by mutation_overlap\n      and frequency (fan-out to all populations).\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_many\"\n    notes: \"Read by all (population) analysis jobs for same chromosome; high reuse.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    name: \"Sifted Variants Text File\"\n    description: >\n      Plain-text file of SIFT-scored variant records for one chromosome, extracted from\n      the annotation VCF by sifting.py. Consumed by mutation_overlap and frequency jobs.\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_many\"\n    notes: \"Read by all (population) analysis jobs for same chromosome; high reuse.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n    name: \"Mutation Overlap Output\"\n    description: >\n      Tarball containing pairwise mutation overlap plots (matplotlib PNG) and text\n      statistics for one (chromosome, population) pair. Named chr{C}-{POP}.tar.gz.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"medium\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once\"\n    notes: \"Final scientific result; one per (chromosome, population) pair.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:frequency_output\"\n    name: \"Frequency Analysis Output\"\n    description: >\n      Collection of 1000 histogram files, 1000 random-individual files, and 1000 PNG\n      plots from Monte Carlo frequency estimation for one (chromosome, population) pair.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"mixed\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once\"\n    notes: \"3000 files per job; high file-count output; one set per (chromosome, population) pair.\"\n\npc_edges:\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals\"\n    consumer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"n_to_1\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"N chunk tarballs (N=ind_jobs) gathered into one merge job per chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One merged archive broadcast to all population-level mutation_overlap jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One merged archive broadcast to all population-level frequency jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One sifted variant file broadcast to all population-level mutation_overlap jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One sifted variant file broadcast to all population-level frequency jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\nworkflow_graph:\n  entry_tasks:\n    - \"task:individuals\"\n    - \"task:sifting\"\n  exit_tasks:\n    - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    - \"task:frequency\"\n  critical_path:\n    - \"task:individuals\"\n    - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n  integrity_hash: \"pending_python_execution\"\n  integrity_hash_note: >\n    SHA-256 of canonical JSON of pc_edges sorted by edge_id. Compute via:\n    python3 -c \"import json,hashlib; edges=sorted([{'consumer':'task:individuals_merge','data_objects':['data:individual_chunk_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1','pc_pattern':'n_to_1','producer':'task:individuals'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'}],key=lambda e:e['edge_id']); print(hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(edges,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest())\"\n\nworkflow_patterns:\n  primary_pattern: \"scatter_gather\"\n  secondary_patterns:\n    - \"broadcast\"\n  pattern_notes: >\n    The workflow scatters VCF processing across chromosomes and chunks (embarrassingly parallel\n    extraction), gathers chunks into per-chromosome archives (n_to_1 merge), then broadcasts\n    merged archives and sifted files to all (chromosome, population) analysis jobs. There is\n    no iterative loop; execution is a single-pass DAG.\n  loop_count: 0\n  has_checkpoint_restart: false\n  has_conditional_branches: false\n\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_individuals\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n    severity: \"high\"\n    description: >\n      individuals.py writes 2504 individual text files per VCF chunk before tar-compressing.\n      With ind_jobs chunks per chromosome and 10 chromosomes, total transient small-file writes\n      can reach 250,400 files. POSIX metadata pressure is significant on shared filesystems.\n    recommendation: >\n      Consider writing individual data directly into the tarball via streaming (tarfile module)\n      rather than materializing all 2504 files on disk. Alternatively, use a single HDF5 or\n      Parquet file per chunk to reduce inode pressure.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_chunk_merge\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n    severity: \"medium\"\n    description: >\n      individuals_merge.py extracts all N chunk tarballs to a tempdir, accumulates individual\n      files, then recompresses the entire set. This extract-recompress cycle is O(N*chunk_size)\n      disk I/O. The merged output could instead be built by streaming concatenation.\n    recommendation: >\n      Use tarfile append mode or GNU tar --concatenate to merge archives without full extraction,\n      reducing disk amplification and I/O by approximately N-fold.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n    severity: \"medium\"\n    description: >\n      The merged chromosome tarball (data:merged_chromosome_tar) is read independently by each\n      (chromosome, population) job. With 7 populations per chromosome, the same archive is\n      opened and extracted 7 times for mutation_overlap and 7 times for frequency (14 total reads).\n    recommendation: >\n      Stage the merged tarball to a burst buffer or node-local SSD before launching population\n      analysis jobs. Alternatively, co-schedule all population jobs on nodes sharing local storage\n      to benefit from OS page cache.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_sifted_chr_txt\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n    severity: \"low\"\n    description: >\n      The sifted variants file (data:sifted_chr_txt) is read by all (chromosome, population)\n      analysis jobs (14 reads per chromosome). File is small so overhead is low, but caching\n      or broadcast staging would eliminate repeated PFS lookups.\n    recommendation: >\n      Pre-stage sifted variant files to node-local storage or ramdisk before population\n      analysis phase. Low priority given small file size.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_frequency_output\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n    severity: \"high\"\n    description: >\n      frequency.py writes 3000 output files per job (1000 histograms + 1000 random-individual\n      files + 1000 PNG plots). With 10 chromosomes * 7 populations = 70 jobs, total output\n      files reach ~210,000. This is severe metadata overhead on shared PFS.\n    recommendation: >\n      Consolidate frequency output into a single HDF5 or NetCDF file per job, or package\n      all 3000 files into a tarball before writing to shared storage.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_sifting_temp\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n    severity: \"low\"\n    description: >\n      sifting.py writes a temp VCF file (SIFT.chr{C}.vcf) via subprocess grep, reads it\n      back in Python, then deletes it. This intermediate file could be replaced with a\n      subprocess pipe directly into Python for in-memory filtering.\n    recommendation: >\n      Replace the write-read-delete pattern with subprocess.Popen + communicate() or\n      subprocess.run(stdout=PIPE) to pipe grep output directly into Python without disk I/O.\n\nexecution_profiles:\n  - profile_id: \"exec:full\"\n    name: \"Full Workflow\"\n    description: \"All 5 tasks across all chromosomes and populations.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    notes: \"Default Pegasus DAX execution; 10 chromosomes * ind_jobs chunks + 10 merge + 10 sift + 70 analysis jobs.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:individuals_only\"\n    name: \"Individuals Extraction Only\"\n    description: \"Run only VCF extraction to individual chunk tarballs.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    notes: \"Useful for pre-staging individual data; produces data:individual_chunk_tar.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:sifting_only\"\n    name: \"Sifting Only\"\n    description: \"Run only variant sifting on annotation VCFs.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    notes: \"Produces SIFT-filtered variant lists; independent of individuals pipeline.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:population_analysis_only\"\n    name: \"Population Analysis Only\"\n    description: \"Run mutation_overlap and frequency assuming merged archives and sifted files already exist.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    notes: \"Requires data:merged_chromosome_tar and data:sifted_chr_txt to be pre-staged.\"\n\ntranslation_metadata:\n  source_wms: \"pegasus\"\n  source_executor: \"htcondor\"\n  translation_tool: \"claude-sonnet-4-6 static analysis\"\n  translation_date: \"2026-03-04\"\n  analysis_method: \"static\"\n  files_analyzed:\n    - \"daxgen.py\"\n    - \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    - \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    - \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    - \"bin/mutation_overlap.py\"\n    - \"bin/frequency.py\"\n    - \"data.csv\"\n    - \"README.md\"\n  field_confidence_records:\n    - field: \"stages\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Stage boundaries directly inferred from daxgen.py dependency graph structure.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].parallelism_model\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Loop structure in daxgen.py makes per-chromosome and per-population fan-out explicit.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].io_dominance\"\n      confidence: 0.80\n      rationale: \"Inferred from code logic; no profiling data available.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].io_access_type\"\n      confidence: 0.90\n      rationale: \"No MPI, HDF5, or collective I/O imports found; all access is standard Python file I/O.\"\n    - field: \"data_objects[].volume_class\"\n      confidence: 0.70\n      rationale: \"Estimated from VCF row counts (250000) and individual counts (2504); no runtime measurements.\"\n    - field: \"pc_edges[].coupling\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Pegasus WMS manages all data staging; tasks communicate exclusively via files.\"\n    - field: \"workflow_patterns\"\n      confidence: 0.90\n      rationale: \"DAG structure clearly shows scatter (chunks) + gather (merge) + broadcast (fan-out to populations).\"\n    - field: \"io_behavioral_hints\"\n      confidence: 0.85\n      rationale: \"Small file patterns (2504 files/job, 3000 files/job) and extract-recompress cycle observed directly in code.\"\n    - field: \"integrity_hash\"\n      confidence: 0.0\n      rationale: \"Python execution not available during static analysis; hash is pending.\"\n  unmapped_pegasus_features:\n    - feature: \"decaf_mode\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--decaf\"\n      description: \"Optional Decaf in-memory MPI dataflow between tasks; not reflected in canonical WDD (deployment detail).\"\n    - feature: \"pmc_mode\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--pmc\"\n      description: \"Pegasus MPI Cluster task clustering; groups jobs into MPI ranks; deployment detail not in WDD.\"\n    - feature: \"bypass_staging\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--bypass\"\n      description: \"Pegasus bypass staging for annotation VCFs; runtime optimization, not workflow structure.\"\n"}},{"tool_name":"Edit","tool_use_id":"toolu_013L3pbTy4r94gfzp2fJFcJ2","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_wdd/1000genome-wdd-claude-trial2.yaml","old_string":"python3 -c \"import json,hashlib; edges=[...]; print(hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(edges,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest())\"\n","new_string":"schema_version: \"wrd-7.0\"\n\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: \"wrd:1000genome\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  version_notes: \"Initial WDD compiled from daxgen.py and bin/ task scripts via static analysis.\"\n  deprecated: false\n  workflow_name: \"1000genome\"\n  workflow_description: >\n    The 1000 Genomes workflow identifies mutational overlaps and allele frequency distributions\n    in human genomic data from the 1000 Genomes Project. It processes per-chromosome VCF files\n    through individual extraction, merging, variant sifting (SIFT scores), pairwise mutation\n    overlap analysis, and Monte Carlo frequency estimation across 26 super-populations.\n    Implemented as a Pegasus WMS DAX workflow (daxgen.py) targeting HTCondor.\n  source_format: \"compiled_from_pegasus_dax\"\n  source_file: \"daxgen.py\"\n  generated_by: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n  analysis_date: \"2026-03-04\"\n  source_commit: \"static_analysis_no_git_hash\"\n  workflow_domain: \"genomics\"\n  target_system_class: \"hpc_cluster\"\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n    stage_name: \"Individuals Extraction\"\n    stage_description: >\n      For each chromosome, split the VCF file into N chunks and extract per-individual\n      variant data from each chunk, producing compressed tarball outputs.\n    order: 1\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    stage_name: \"Merge and Sifting\"\n    stage_description: >\n      Merge per-chunk individual tarballs into a single per-chromosome archive, and in\n      parallel extract SIFT-scored variants from the annotation VCF. Both sub-tasks run\n      concurrently per chromosome.\n    order: 2\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    stage_name: \"Population Analysis\"\n    stage_description: >\n      For each (chromosome, population) pair, run pairwise mutation overlap analysis and\n      Monte Carlo allele frequency estimation using the merged chromosome archive and\n      sifted variant list as inputs.\n    order: 3\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals\"\n    task_name: \"individuals\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:individuals_extraction\"\n    description: >\n      Reads a VCF chunk (by line range), extracts per-individual genotype data for all\n      2504 individuals, writes individual text files, and compresses them into a tarball\n      named chr{C}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz. Idempotent: re-running overwrites the same output.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: \"param:ind_jobs\"\n      notes: \"One job per VCF chunk per chromosome; chunks are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n      - \"data:columns_txt\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 512\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Reads entire VCF chunk into memory; writes 2504 small files then tar-compresses.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    task_name: \"individuals_merge\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Merges all per-chunk tarballs for a chromosome into a single archive chr{C}n.tar.gz.\n      Extracts all chunk tarballs into a temporary directory, accumulates individual files,\n      and recompresses. Transient disk amplification is significant (all chunks extracted).\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: 1\n      notes: \"One merge job per chromosome; merge jobs for different chromosomes are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 1024\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Disk amplification: all chunk tarballs must be extracted simultaneously in tempdir.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:sifting\"\n    task_name: \"sifting\"\n    executable: \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Extracts SIFT-scored variants from the annotation VCF using subprocess grep to a\n      temporary file, then filters by regex. Writes SIFT.chr{C}.vcf as an intermediate,\n      then removes it after reading back. Produces a plain-text sifted variant list.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances_per_chromosome: 1\n      notes: \"One sifting job per chromosome; independent across chromosomes.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 256\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"Uses subprocess grep to temp file then Python regex post-filter; temp file deleted after use.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    task_name: \"mutation_overlap\"\n    executable: \"bin/mutation_overlap.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Computes pairwise mutation overlap (set intersection) across all individuals in a\n      population for a given chromosome. Reads merged chromosome tar at startup. Performs\n      O(N^2) pairwise comparisons. Generates matplotlib plots and text statistics, packaged\n      into chr{C}-{POP}.tar.gz.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances: \"param:n_chromosomes * param:n_populations\"\n      notes: \"One job per (chromosome, population) pair; all pairs are independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 2048\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"O(N^2) pairwise; N=population size (up to 2504). Reads full merged tar at startup.\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:frequency\"\n    task_name: \"frequency\"\n    executable: \"bin/frequency.py\"\n    stage_ref: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Runs 1000 Monte Carlo iterations of allele frequency estimation (n=52 random\n      individuals per draw) for a (chromosome, population) pair. Reads merged chromosome\n      tar at module-level. Writes 1000 histograms + 1000 random-individual files + 1000\n      PNG plots per job.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      instances: \"param:n_chromosomes * param:n_populations\"\n      notes: \"One job per (chromosome, population) pair; independent.\"\n    io_dominance: \"compute_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:frequency_output\"\n    runtime_hints:\n      memory_per_instance_mb: 1024\n      cpu_cores: 1\n      notes: \"1000 iterations; n_indiv=52; writes 3000 output files per job (high file count).\"\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n    name: \"Chromosome VCF\"\n    description: >\n      Input VCF file for one chromosome (e.g., ALL.chr1.250000.vcf). Contains genotype\n      data for all 2504 individuals at 250000 variant sites. One file per chromosome.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"10 chromosomes in data.csv; each ~250000 variant rows.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:columns_txt\"\n    name: \"Columns File\"\n    description: >\n      Text file listing column indices or individual IDs used by individuals.py to select\n      the 2504 individual columns from the VCF.\n    category: \"config\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"Static configuration; read once per individuals job.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    name: \"Annotation VCF\"\n    description: >\n      VEP-annotated VCF file per chromosome (e.g., ALL.chrN.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf).\n      Contains SIFT functional effect predictions used by sifting.py.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"One per chromosome; grep-filtered by sifting.py.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:population_file\"\n    name: \"Population Definition File\"\n    description: >\n      Text file listing individual IDs belonging to one super-population (e.g., AFR, EUR).\n      Used by mutation_overlap.py and frequency.py to filter individuals. 7 population\n      files referenced in daxgen.py.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"sequential_read\"\n    notes: \"7 super-population files; each consumed by multiple downstream jobs.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    name: \"Individual Chunk Tarball\"\n    description: >\n      Compressed tarball of per-individual variant text files for one VCF chunk of one\n      chromosome. Named chr{C}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz. Produced by individuals.py.\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"stage_scoped\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"medium\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_once\"\n    notes: \"N tarballs per chromosome (N=ind_jobs); consumed by individuals_merge.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    name: \"Merged Chromosome Tarball\"\n    description: >\n      Single merged tarball of all individual variant files for one chromosome.\n      Named chr{C}n.tar.gz. Produced by individuals_merge; consumed by mutation_overlap\n      and frequency (fan-out to all populations).\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_many\"\n    notes: \"Read by all (population) analysis jobs for same chromosome; high reuse.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    name: \"Sifted Variants Text File\"\n    description: >\n      Plain-text file of SIFT-scored variant records for one chromosome, extracted from\n      the annotation VCF by sifting.py. Consumed by mutation_overlap and frequency jobs.\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format: \"txt\"\n    volume_class: \"small\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once_read_many\"\n    notes: \"Read by all (population) analysis jobs for same chromosome; high reuse.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:mutation_overlap_output\"\n    name: \"Mutation Overlap Output\"\n    description: >\n      Tarball containing pairwise mutation overlap plots (matplotlib PNG) and text\n      statistics for one (chromosome, population) pair. Named chr{C}-{POP}.tar.gz.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    volume_class: \"medium\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once\"\n    notes: \"Final scientific result; one per (chromosome, population) pair.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:frequency_output\"\n    name: \"Frequency Analysis Output\"\n    description: >\n      Collection of 1000 histogram files, 1000 random-individual files, and 1000 PNG\n      plots from Monte Carlo frequency estimation for one (chromosome, population) pair.\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format: \"mixed\"\n    volume_class: \"large\"\n    access_pattern: \"write_once\"\n    notes: \"3000 files per job; high file-count output; one set per (chromosome, population) pair.\"\n\npc_edges:\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals\"\n    consumer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:individual_chunk_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"n_to_1\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"N chunk tarballs (N=ind_jobs) gathered into one merge job per chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One merged archive broadcast to all population-level mutation_overlap jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One merged archive broadcast to all population-level frequency jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One sifted variant file broadcast to all population-level mutation_overlap jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    coupling: \"loose\"\n    communication_pattern: \"shared_file\"\n    notes: \"One sifted variant file broadcast to all population-level frequency jobs for same chromosome.\"\n\nworkflow_graph:\n  entry_tasks:\n    - \"task:individuals\"\n    - \"task:sifting\"\n  exit_tasks:\n    - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    - \"task:frequency\"\n  critical_path:\n    - \"task:individuals\"\n    - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n  integrity_hash: \"pending_python_execution\"\n  integrity_hash_note: >\n    SHA-256 of canonical JSON of pc_edges sorted by edge_id. Compute via:\n    python3 -c \"import json,hashlib; edges=sorted([{'consumer':'task:individuals_merge','data_objects':['data:individual_chunk_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1','pc_pattern':'n_to_1','producer':'task:individuals'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:merged_chromosome_tar'],'edge_id':'pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:individuals_merge'},{'consumer':'task:frequency','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'},{'consumer':'task:mutation_overlap','data_objects':['data:sifted_chr_txt'],'edge_id':'pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n','pc_pattern':'1_to_n','producer':'task:sifting'}],key=lambda e:e['edge_id']); print(hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(edges,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest())\"\n\nworkflow_patterns:\n  primary_pattern: \"scatter_gather\"\n  secondary_patterns:\n    - \"broadcast\"\n  pattern_notes: >\n    The workflow scatters VCF processing across chromosomes and chunks (embarrassingly parallel\n    extraction), gathers chunks into per-chromosome archives (n_to_1 merge), then broadcasts\n    merged archives and sifted files to all (chromosome, population) analysis jobs. There is\n    no iterative loop; execution is a single-pass DAG.\n  loop_count: 0\n  has_checkpoint_restart: false\n  has_conditional_branches: false\n\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_individuals\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n    severity: \"high\"\n    description: >\n      individuals.py writes 2504 individual text files per VCF chunk before tar-compressing.\n      With ind_jobs chunks per chromosome and 10 chromosomes, total transient small-file writes\n      can reach 250,400 files. POSIX metadata pressure is significant on shared filesystems.\n    recommendation: >\n      Consider writing individual data directly into the tarball via streaming (tarfile module)\n      rather than materializing all 2504 files on disk. Alternatively, use a single HDF5 or\n      Parquet file per chunk to reduce inode pressure.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_chunk_merge\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n    severity: \"medium\"\n    description: >\n      individuals_merge.py extracts all N chunk tarballs to a tempdir, accumulates individual\n      files, then recompresses the entire set. This extract-recompress cycle is O(N*chunk_size)\n      disk I/O. The merged output could instead be built by streaming concatenation.\n    recommendation: >\n      Use tarfile append mode or GNU tar --concatenate to merge archives without full extraction,\n      reducing disk amplification and I/O by approximately N-fold.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_merged_chromosome_tar\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n    severity: \"medium\"\n    description: >\n      The merged chromosome tarball (data:merged_chromosome_tar) is read independently by each\n      (chromosome, population) job. With 7 populations per chromosome, the same archive is\n      opened and extracted 7 times for mutation_overlap and 7 times for frequency (14 total reads).\n    recommendation: >\n      Stage the merged tarball to a burst buffer or node-local SSD before launching population\n      analysis jobs. Alternatively, co-schedule all population jobs on nodes sharing local storage\n      to benefit from OS page cache.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:data_reuse_sifted_chr_txt\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\n    severity: \"low\"\n    description: >\n      The sifted variants file (data:sifted_chr_txt) is read by all (chromosome, population)\n      analysis jobs (14 reads per chromosome). File is small so overhead is low, but caching\n      or broadcast staging would eliminate repeated PFS lookups.\n    recommendation: >\n      Pre-stage sifted variant files to node-local storage or ramdisk before population\n      analysis phase. Low priority given small file size.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:small_file_overhead_frequency_output\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n    severity: \"high\"\n    description: >\n      frequency.py writes 3000 output files per job (1000 histograms + 1000 random-individual\n      files + 1000 PNG plots). With 10 chromosomes * 7 populations = 70 jobs, total output\n      files reach ~210,000. This is severe metadata overhead on shared PFS.\n    recommendation: >\n      Consolidate frequency output into a single HDF5 or NetCDF file per job, or package\n      all 3000 files into a tarball before writing to shared storage.\n\n  - hint_id: \"hint:unnecessary_serialization_sifting_temp\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    potential_concern: \"unnecessary_serialization\"\n    severity: \"low\"\n    description: >\n      sifting.py writes a temp VCF file (SIFT.chr{C}.vcf) via subprocess grep, reads it\n      back in Python, then deletes it. This intermediate file could be replaced with a\n      subprocess pipe directly into Python for in-memory filtering.\n    recommendation: >\n      Replace the write-read-delete pattern with subprocess.Popen + communicate() or\n      subprocess.run(stdout=PIPE) to pipe grep output directly into Python without disk I/O.\n\nexecution_profiles:\n  - profile_id: \"exec:full\"\n    name: \"Full Workflow\"\n    description: \"All 5 tasks across all chromosomes and populations.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    notes: \"Default Pegasus DAX execution; 10 chromosomes * ind_jobs chunks + 10 merge + 10 sift + 70 analysis jobs.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:individuals_only\"\n    name: \"Individuals Extraction Only\"\n    description: \"Run only VCF extraction to individual chunk tarballs.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    notes: \"Useful for pre-staging individual data; produces data:individual_chunk_tar.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:sifting_only\"\n    name: \"Sifting Only\"\n    description: \"Run only variant sifting on annotation VCFs.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n    notes: \"Produces SIFT-filtered variant lists; independent of individuals pipeline.\"\n\n  - profile_id: \"exec:population_analysis_only\"\n    name: \"Population Analysis Only\"\n    description: \"Run mutation_overlap and frequency assuming merged archives and sifted files already exist.\"\n    tasks_included:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    notes: \"Requires data:merged_chromosome_tar and data:sifted_chr_txt to be pre-staged.\"\n\ntranslation_metadata:\n  source_wms: \"pegasus\"\n  source_executor: \"htcondor\"\n  translation_tool: \"claude-sonnet-4-6 static analysis\"\n  translation_date: \"2026-03-04\"\n  analysis_method: \"static\"\n  files_analyzed:\n    - \"daxgen.py\"\n    - \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    - \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    - \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    - \"bin/mutation_overlap.py\"\n    - \"bin/frequency.py\"\n    - \"data.csv\"\n    - \"README.md\"\n  field_confidence_records:\n    - field: \"stages\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Stage boundaries directly inferred from daxgen.py dependency graph structure.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].parallelism_model\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Loop structure in daxgen.py makes per-chromosome and per-population fan-out explicit.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].io_dominance\"\n      confidence: 0.80\n      rationale: \"Inferred from code logic; no profiling data available.\"\n    - field: \"tasks[].io_access_type\"\n      confidence: 0.90\n      rationale: \"No MPI, HDF5, or collective I/O imports found; all access is standard Python file I/O.\"\n    - field: \"data_objects[].volume_class\"\n      confidence: 0.70\n      rationale: \"Estimated from VCF row counts (250000) and individual counts (2504); no runtime measurements.\"\n    - field: \"pc_edges[].coupling\"\n      confidence: 0.95\n      rationale: \"Pegasus WMS manages all data staging; tasks communicate exclusively via files.\"\n    - field: \"workflow_patterns\"\n      confidence: 0.90\n      rationale: \"DAG structure clearly shows scatter (chunks) + gather (merge) + broadcast (fan-out to populations).\"\n    - field: \"io_behavioral_hints\"\n      confidence: 0.85\n      rationale: \"Small file patterns (2504 files/job, 3000 files/job) and extract-recompress cycle observed directly in code.\"\n    - field: \"integrity_hash\"\n      confidence: 0.0\n      rationale: \"Python execution not available during static analysis; hash is pending.\"\n  unmapped_pegasus_features:\n    - feature: \"decaf_mode\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--decaf\"\n      description: \"Optional Decaf in-memory MPI dataflow between tasks; not reflected in canonical WDD (deployment detail).\"\n    - feature: \"pmc_mode\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--pmc\"\n      description: \"Pegasus MPI Cluster task clustering; groups jobs into MPI ranks; deployment detail not in WDD.\"\n    - feature: \"bypass_staging\"\n      daxgen_flag: \"--bypass\"\n      description: \"Pegasus bypass staging for annotation VCFs; runtime optimization, not workflow structure.\"\n","replace_all":false}}],"uuid":"18d2ef1e-e930-4063-a776-ddb6d5d75863"}
